1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,039
ChatGPT once made up court

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:02,480
cases.

3
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:03,620
Not one.

4
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,040
A whole list.

5
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:07,519
And a real lawyer handed them to

6
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,200
a real judge.

7
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,300
The judge looked them up.

8
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:11,740
They didn't exist.

9
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:13,919
And when the lawyer asked it, Is

10
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,900
this case real?", it said yes.

11
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:18,379
Last time, we saw that AI

12
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:20,339
guesses what sounds right, not

13
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:20,880
what is right.

14
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:22,800
Here, those two split apart.

15
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:24,640
Why would it do that?

16
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:26,700
Let's un-jargon it.

17
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:29,300
It wasn't lying.

18
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,440
Lying means you know the truth.

19
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:33,739
It was guessing, like a student

20
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,400
bluffing in a closed book exam.

21
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,799
When an AI makes something up

22
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,619
and says it like a fact, that's

23
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,740
called a hallucination.

24
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:42,699
Odd word, because it isn't

25
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:43,340
seeing things.

26
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:44,660
It's bluffing.

27
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:46,480
So, three questions.

28
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:48,779
Why does AI make things up at

29
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:49,020
all?

30
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:50,820
Why does it sound so sure?

31
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:52,800
And how do you protect yourself?

32
00:00:53,567 --> 00:00:54,287
Question one.

33
00:00:55,027 --> 00:00:56,146
Why does it make things up at

34
00:00:56,147 --> 00:00:56,527
all?

35
00:00:57,347 --> 00:00:57,787
Quick test.

36
00:00:58,507 --> 00:01:00,206
You're in an exam, and there's

37
00:01:00,207 --> 00:01:01,686
one question you have no clue

38
00:01:01,687 --> 00:01:02,067
about.

39
00:01:02,647 --> 00:01:03,307
Leave it blank?

40
00:01:04,027 --> 00:01:04,807
Zero points.

41
00:01:05,347 --> 00:01:06,107
Make a guess?

42
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:07,647
You might get lucky.

43
00:01:08,467 --> 00:01:09,367
You'd guess, right?

44
00:01:10,027 --> 00:01:10,747
Everyone does.

45
00:01:11,787 --> 00:01:13,207
AI learns the same way.

46
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:15,226
It answers millions of practice

47
00:01:15,227 --> 00:01:16,906
questions, and each one is

48
00:01:16,907 --> 00:01:17,307
marked.

49
00:01:17,987 --> 00:01:18,807
Right: one point.

50
00:01:19,307 --> 00:01:20,307
Wrong: zero.

51
00:01:20,967 --> 00:01:22,447
I don't know": also zero.

52
00:01:23,027 --> 00:01:24,886
Over time, it gets pushed toward

53
00:01:24,887 --> 00:01:25,907
whatever scores points.

54
00:01:26,427 --> 00:01:27,467
And guessing scores.

55
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:29,347
I don't know never does.

56
00:01:30,107 --> 00:01:31,926
So it learns one habit: always

57
00:01:31,927 --> 00:01:32,427
answer.

58
00:01:33,807 --> 00:01:35,606
Researchers at OpenAI, the

59
00:01:35,607 --> 00:01:38,026
company behind ChatGPT, showed

60
00:01:38,027 --> 00:01:39,167
this in 2025.

61
00:01:39,927 --> 00:01:41,526
They asked an AI for one of

62
00:01:41,527 --> 00:01:43,366
their birthdays and said: only

63
00:01:43,367 --> 00:01:44,347
answer if you know.

64
00:01:44,887 --> 00:01:45,547
Three tries.

65
00:01:46,307 --> 00:01:47,367
Three different dates.

66
00:01:47,947 --> 00:01:48,487
All wrong.

67
00:01:49,127 --> 00:01:51,486
So, answer one: it's trained to

68
00:01:51,487 --> 00:01:52,207
always answer.

69
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:57,060
Question two.

70
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:58,940
Why does it sound so sure?

71
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,319
Think about how people talk when

72
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:02,100
they're not sure.

73
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:02,880
Um…

74
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:04,799
I think it's…

75
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:05,680
maybe Tuesday?

76
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,440
You can hear the doubt.

77
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:09,780
That wobble is a warning sign.

78
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,840
AI doesn't wobble.

79
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:14,079
Remember, it builds every answer

80
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:15,839
one guess at a time, and it

81
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,400
makes every guess the same way,

82
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,520
true or not.

83
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,939
So a real fact and a made up one

84
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:22,400
come out in the same calm,

85
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:23,440
friendly voice.

86
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,859
That's how an airline's chatbot

87
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:27,999
in Canada told a man whose

88
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,059
grandmother had just died that

89
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:31,279
he could claim a funeral

90
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,140
discount later.

91
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:34,239
The airline's own website said

92
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:34,720
the opposite.

93
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,080
A tribunal made the airline pay.

94
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:39,679
So, answer two: it never

95
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,060
wobbles, even when it's wrong.

96
00:02:41,733 --> 00:02:42,553
Question three.

97
00:02:43,333 --> 00:02:44,373
How do you protect yourself?

98
00:02:45,093 --> 00:02:45,653
Three habits.

99
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:48,632
One: ask for sources, and then

100
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:49,673
actually open them.

101
00:02:50,133 --> 00:02:51,033
Remember the lawyer?

102
00:02:51,673 --> 00:02:53,372
He asked for cases, and got

103
00:02:53,373 --> 00:02:53,813
cases.

104
00:02:54,453 --> 00:02:55,553
They just weren't real.

105
00:02:56,173 --> 00:02:57,132
A link you haven't clicked

106
00:02:57,133 --> 00:02:57,913
proves nothing.

107
00:02:58,673 --> 00:03:00,533
Two: make it an open book exam.

108
00:03:01,473 --> 00:03:02,792
Paste in the real thing, the

109
00:03:02,793 --> 00:03:04,493
letter, the webpage, the rules,

110
00:03:04,793 --> 00:03:06,452
and ask it to answer only from

111
00:03:06,453 --> 00:03:06,753
that.

112
00:03:07,233 --> 00:03:08,932
It guesses far less when the

113
00:03:08,933 --> 00:03:10,392
answer is right in front of it.

114
00:03:10,393 --> 00:03:11,333
Far less.

115
00:03:12,093 --> 00:03:12,713
Not never.

116
00:03:13,733 --> 00:03:15,033
Three: double check names,

117
00:03:15,393 --> 00:03:16,473
numbers, dates and quotes.

118
00:03:17,073 --> 00:03:18,013
That's where bluffs hide:

119
00:03:18,593 --> 00:03:19,972
there's only one right answer,

120
00:03:19,973 --> 00:03:21,772
and lots of wrong ones that

121
00:03:21,773 --> 00:03:22,853
sound just as good.

122
00:03:23,433 --> 00:03:24,213
Like that birthday.

123
00:03:25,253 --> 00:03:27,172
So, answer three: open the

124
00:03:27,173 --> 00:03:28,572
sources, give it the book, and

125
00:03:28,573 --> 00:03:29,353
check the details.

126
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,900
So, why does AI hallucinate?

127
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:34,239
It's a guesser, marked like a

128
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,939
student in an exam where a blank

129
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:36,740
scores zero.

130
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:37,940
So it bluffs.

131
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:40,499
And right answers and wrong ones

132
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:41,999
come out in the same confident

133
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,899
voice, so you can't hear the

134
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:44,300
difference.

135
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:46,879
Sounding sure is not the same as

136
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:47,420
being right.

137
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,719
So treat it like a very fast

138
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:51,200
student, not an expert.

139
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:52,479
Give it the book.

140
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:54,020
And check its work.

141
00:03:54,767 --> 00:03:56,647
But so far, AI only talks.

142
00:03:57,307 --> 00:03:58,426
What happens when it can act,

143
00:03:58,427 --> 00:04:00,186
and book the flight, send the

144
00:04:00,187 --> 00:04:01,307
email, spend the money?

145
00:04:01,847 --> 00:04:03,546
That's called an AI agent, and

146
00:04:03,547 --> 00:04:04,047
it's next.

147
00:04:05,407 --> 00:04:06,407
Subscribe so you don't miss it.
